<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34243" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμ-πάσσω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμ-ττω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πάσω [ᾰ</span>]:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sprinkle in</i> or <i>on</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι ἔς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Lap.</u>
					67
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς τέφρας</span> some
			<i>powder</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ly.</u>
				210a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					11.134
				</span></i>
			: in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only metaph., <i>weave</i> rich patterns <i>in</i> a web
			of cloth, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέας δ᾽ ἐνέπασσεν ἀέθλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.126
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				22.441
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
